# Charts tab = Deriv `#chart` only

Reference: **https://bot.deriv.com/#chart** (Chrome). Match Deriv’s chart window — **no more, no less**.

## Definition of done (check all before commit/push)

1. **Layout**: Full-page chart desk only. **No** Bot Builder run bar, Summary/Transactions/Journal, or wallet on the Charts nav tab.
2. **Market selector**: SmartCharts `ChartTitle` — left categories (Favorites, Derived → Synthetics, etc.), right symbol list with search and favorites. Must not flicker while ticks update.
3. **Toolbar**: Chart type, Studies, Views, Draw tools, Share/Download visible and working (same bundle as `SmartChart` — no async orphan chunks).
4. **Live chart**: Line/candles move on synthetic symbols (e.g. `R_100` / 1s indices). Verify WS ticks in Chrome DevTools.
5. **Last-digit panel**: Enabled on synthetic/volatility symbols (`showLastDigitStats` + `isSyntheticChartSymbol`).
6. **Verify in Chrome** at `http://localhost:3000/dashboard` → Charts tab. Compare side-by-side with Deriv. List anything still missing in the PR/commit message.

## Do not

- Ship “chart loads” or “flicker fixed” as complete without the checklist above.
- **Remove the Bot Builder chart modal** or replace it with nav to Charts tab — Deriv keeps builder context; toolbar Charts opens a **full-viewport overlay**, not a tab switch.
- Embed the Charts **nav tab** layout inside Bot Builder shell (run bar + chart side-by-side) when SmartCharts `ChartTitle` exists.
- Re-request `active_symbols` on every symbol change (once per session unless list empty).
- Pass unstable props into `<SmartChart>` on every tick (`topWidgets`, `subscribeQuotes`, inline `settings` objects) — use refs/memo.

## Key files

- `SmartChartDesk.tsx` — Charts tab shell (must stay chart-only)
- `SmartChartRuntime.tsx` — single chunk: SmartChart + toolbar widgets
- `SmartChartPanel.tsx` / `useSmartChartFeed.ts` — feed + stable callbacks
- `lib/chart/active-symbols.ts` — symbol reference data
- `DashboardClient.tsx` — `case "chart"` must render `SmartChartDesk`, not builder desk

## Browser

Google Chrome only for manual QA (see `chrome-browser.mdc`).
